{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 2090 (commit 62e4245a93f on impl-2e0f, from origin/main 960fbfef2f).\n\nPlan review PASSED (signable, signed at head 960fbfef2f) after two remediation rounds; ticket claimed.\n\nWhat landed:\n- `registry.content_triggered_overlays` gains a keyword-only `changed_files` sequence; `overlay_union` (`workflow_ops.py`) passes the step's changed-file list through and its `description=` now names the added-declaration trigger.\n- New `_has_added_declaration` + `_content_selects_tests` helpers: an added line matching the existing polyglot `_REMOVED_DECL_RE`, whose DECLARED NAME the same file does not also remove, with no changed file under the `tests` globs. A separate `_DECL_NAME_RE` does the name extraction (`_REMOVED_DECL_RE` has no capture group) and matches the Go receiver form `func (s *Store) Compute(` by its method name, not its receiver. Anonymous declarations yield no name and are skipped, so the trigger fails closed.\n- Path predicates are the committed `tests` globs plus a docs/data extension skip — no `src/**` and no Python-only regex, so it fires for a Ruby, Java, Next.js or .NET target.\n- Guard (vii) in `code-review-tests.md` narrowed with diff-decidable definitions; eval corpus gains `R-newbehaviour-named-violating-input` and `FP-preexisting-code-gap-no-new-behaviour`.\n\nTests: `tests/unit/test_code_review_tests_trigger.py`, 28 cases, all mutation-checked. Eleven mutations each killed a specific test: dropping the removed-name suppression (kills the 1703 replay), never suppressing on a changed test file, dropping the docs/data extension skip, swapping the added/removed buckets, dropping per-file provenance (kills the move replay), removing the trigger entirely, not passing changed_files into the step, weakening the guard-(vii) wording, giving anonymous declarations a synthetic name, blanking the step description, and dropping the Go-receiver alternative.\n\nGates green in the worktree: make lint, make typecheck, check_complexity_baseline --check (new=0 increased=0), check_criteria_vocabulary, registry.py at 695 lines against the 800 cap, and 412 tests across every tests/unit/test_code_review_*.py plus the vocabulary and prompt-index suites."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787383880956533001,"uuid":"7a2d56ba-edea-4087-8c8b-8ad822a63bae"}